{"w":2400,"h":3390,"lines":[{"c":1,"h":0.035549296601331992,"x":0.008138018200897601,"t":"@MirsIELTS","y":0.0054811656404017972,"w":0.30405250549316404},{"c":1,"x":0.67556468254998525,"y":0.040697674522817029,"t":"Sample Writing answers","h":0.015988371857499573,"w":0.23203285217285163},{"y":0.08538393033106606,"w":0.72721054077148439,"h":0.02413873588089388,"x":0.11692117194947826,"c":1,"t":"Ideas are easy to follow and logically organised. Linking expressions are well"},{"c":1,"y":0.10465116281252818,"h":0.017472730766003863,"t":"integrated [Whether | Sometimes | Perhaps] and generally accurate, and cohesive","x":0.11909650832798226,"w":0.77207392374674477},{"h":0.015988371857499684,"x":0.1190965003521427,"t":"devices are used well [Many tend to | everybody who] with some errors [own","y":0.12354651174079423,"c":1,"w":0.72073923746744795},{"x":0.11909652078511404,"y":0.14098837211198512,"h":0.017441860412777732,"w":0.75975357055664061,"c":1,"t":"choices \/ their own choices]. Paragraphing at the start is appropriate, but the last"},{"x":0.11698858137486733,"t":"four sentences are set out separately and inappropriately, which affects the score.","y":0.15806815130717067,"c":1,"w":0.77423395792643224,"h":0.02054183194770931},{"c":1,"x":0.11901161068636885,"w":0.78867563883463532,"h":0.0192479586530927,"y":0.18694973107278556,"t":"There is some higher-level vocabulary, with effective collocation [full of enthusiasm |"},{"w":0.78850102742513017,"x":0.11909650888029129,"t":"tend to live in the present | settle down | unforeseen expenses]. The candidate uses","y":0.20639534894953293,"h":0.0160235300879914,"c":1},{"y":0.22383720932415607,"w":0.75359344482421875,"h":0.017460725722411419,"c":1,"x":0.11909650132597638,"t":"a variety of structures, including comparative forms [rather than | do you prefer],"},{"t":"conditionals [\/f] and a range of multi-clause sentences. Errors remain, with some","y":0.23976732700650694,"x":0.11903274501691859,"h":0.020728044312963712,"c":1,"w":0.75783452351888014},{"t":"missing punctuation and incorrect tenses [be found out \/ find out] and prepositions","x":0.1190415489474817,"w":0.77219024658203139,"h":0.019418875095063681,"y":0.25840777321132102,"c":1},{"y":0.27615349425617919,"h":0.021499084652701006,"x":0.11695176498211916,"c":1,"t":"[In any age \/ At any age], but this does not affect the reader's understanding.","w":0.72706527709960944},{"c":1,"x":0.11901383916405953,"y":0.30557284229096937,"w":0.70658421834309904,"h":0.021449657879044626,"t":"To achieve a higher score, the candidate should ensure that the conclusion"},{"w":0.72708923339843745,"h":0.021202656793735009,"y":0.32280193674323854,"t":"summarises the main ideas, and use effective paragraphing, especially in the","x":0.11900032241868493,"c":1},{"w":0.26935877482096354,"c":1,"h":0.017574725530843827,"t":"second half of the response.","x":0.12098250382537122,"y":0.34336479883337667},{"w":0.036960986455281564,"h":0.013081394746943587,"c":1,"t":"135","x":0.87268993788722815,"y":0.91569767468107677},{"x":0.51817870217865936,"w":0.45194875081380215,"c":1,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","h":0.047818033674121962,"y":0.93898664245731467}]}